course: dictionary
lesson: 9385
title: Sprain: a hurt joint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To sprain a joint means to hurt it by twisting it suddenly. Your ankle, wrist or knee are joints. The joint swells up and feels painful. Sprain can be a verb, as in «She sprained her wrist», or a noun, as in «a sprain».
explain: Context gives you clues. «For a sprained ankle, rest it, put a cold pack on, raise it and tell an adult.» Sprained describes the injury, and the advice shows what helps: rest, ice, a bandage and raising the hurt part. Doctors call this plan RICE.
explain: A sprain is not the same as a broken bone, but both can hurt badly and both may need a doctor. «Urgent treatment centres deal with things like sprains, small cuts and minor burns.» So a sprain is an injury that can be treated, even if it is serious.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «He hurt his ankle by twisting it suddenly, so he could not walk.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: To sprain means to hurt a joint, such as your ankle, wrist or knee, by twisting it suddenly.
fact: A sprain makes the joint swell and feel painful.
fact: A sprain is the injury itself, as in «a small sprain can turn into weeks out».
fact: RICE is the first-aid plan: Rest, Ice, a bandage, and Raising the limb.
fact: A sprain is different from a broken bone, though both may need a doctor.
exercise: «For a sprained ankle, rest it, put a cold pack on, raise it and tell an adult.» What should you do first for a sprained ankle? | *Rest it | Run on it to make it strong | Walk on it until it stops hurting | Twist it again to check
exercise: A doctor says Sam has a sprain, not a broken bone. What does this mean? | Sam's bone has snapped in two | Sam has forgotten his lunch | Sam has a cold | *Sam hurt a joint by a sudden twist, and the bone is not broken
exercise: Which word is the noun in «A small sprain can turn into weeks out»? | turn | *sprain | can | weeks
test: Which word is the verb form in «She sprained her wrist on the stairs.»? | wrist | stairs | she | *sprained
test: Which step from the RICE plan helps a sprained ankle? | Shout for a teacher | Twist it to test it | *Put a cold pack on it | Run on it to warm it up
exam: What does sprain mean? | To be very tired after school | *To hurt a joint by twisting it suddenly | To go for a walk in the rain | To warm up before a match
